INSERT INTO `ha_term_relationships` (`object_id`,`term_taxonomy_id`,`term_order`) SELECT @translation_id,tt.term_taxonomy_id,0 FROM `ha_term_taxonomy` tt JOIN `ha_terms` t ON t.term_id=tt.term_id WHERE @translation_id IS NOT NULL AND tt.taxonomy='category' AND t.slug='iraq' AND NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM `ha_term_relationships` r WHERE r.object_id=@translation_id AND r.term_taxonomy_id=tt.term_taxonomy_id) LIMIT 1;
INSERT INTO `ha_posts` (`post_author`,`post_date`,`post_date_gmt`,`post_content`,`post_title`,`post_excerpt`,`post_status`,`comment_status`,`ping_status`,`post_name`,`post_modified`,`post_modified_gmt`,`post_parent`,`guid`,`menu_order`,`post_type`,`post_mime_type`,`comment_count`) SELECT 1,NOW(),UTC_TIMESTAMP(),'<h2>The Importance of Selecting the Correct Pipe in Irrigation Systems</h2>\n<p>In local irrigation systems, particularly drip line maintenance and cost, the role of main and sub-mains in ensuring uniform pressure and flow distribution is critical. 110 mm diameter pipes are an ideal option for main lines in medium to large farms due to their high water transmission capacity and reduced pressure drop. The correct selection at this stage directly impacts pressure stability at drip emitters and drip line stability.</p>\n\n<h2>Basic Technical Specifications of 110 mm Threaded Pipe</h2>\n<h3>Material and Polymer Type</h3>\n<p>Threaded pipes are generally manufactured from two main materials: Polyethylene (PE) in various grades such as PE50 or PE80, and occasionally PVC. For drip irrigation, PE pipes are preferred due to their high flexibility against temperature changes and resistance to impact. PE50 pipes have a higher working pressure and are more suitable for main lines connected to high-pressure sources, while PE80 is ideal for sub-lines and medium to low pressures. In addition to material, resistance to chemicals present in the soil also plays a role in material selection.</p>\n\n<h3>Wall Thickness and SDR Ratio</h3>\n<p>One of the most important technical parameters is the SDR (Standard Diameter Ratio) coefficient. This ratio represents the relationship between nominal diameter and wall thickness. The lower the SDR, the thicker the wall and the higher the allowable pressure. For 110 mm pipes, the selection between SDR 21 and 40 is determined based on input pressure and line length. Using a pipe with an inappropriate SDR can lead to leakage at joints or sudden pipe failure. Accurate calculation of this coefficient is essential for each farm condition.</p>\n\n<h3>Connection Type and Pipe Flare</h3>\n<p>Sewn pipes are essentially characterized by having standard threads for fitting connections. For 110mm pipes, threads typically include 2 to 10 or 2 to 14 TPI. Selecting pipes with standard ISO 7-1 threads or the Iranian National Standard ensures that joints close without leakage and at optimal pressure. Care must be taken to ensure compatibility between fitting and pipe materials; for example, brass fittings are suitable for metal pipes, while polymer fittings are appropriate for PE pipes.</p>\n<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="https://navar-abyari.ir/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/navar-article-generated/مشخصات-فنی-لوله-نخدار-110-میلیمتر-راهنمای-انتخاب-تصویر-شاخص.webp" alt="مشخصات فنی لوله نخدار 110 میلیمتر: راهنمای انتخاب - تصویر 1"/><figcaption>product technical specs selection 110mm sewn pipe</figcaption></figure>\n\n\n<h2>Impact of 110mm Pipes on Drip and Tape System Performance</h2>\n<p>Pipe diameter selection must align with the total field flow rate and the number of drippers. If the main line (e.g., 110mm) is significantly larger than required, pressure loss will be negligible but the cost will be higher. If it is too small, severe pressure loss will occur, preventing adequate water delivery to the end of the line and causing crop dryness in that area. Precision at this stage is critical to ensure uniform irrigation across the entire field.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Uniform distribution:</strong> 110mm pipes are excellent for main lines up to 300-400 meters with moderate flow rates. For longer distances, accurate pressure loss calculations using the Darcy-Weisbach formula are required.</li>\n<li><strong>Reduced sedimentation:</strong> Adequate flow in PE pipes prevents the accumulation of suspended particles and sediment at the pipe bottom, directly extending the lifespan of drippers.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Also, for farms using various drip line types and their respective performance, precision in the outlet pressure of 110-to-75 or 75-to-40 fittings is critical to maintain the nominal working pressure of the drippers.</p>\n\n<h2>Practical guide for installation and maintenance of 110 threaded pipe</h2>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Correct cutting:</strong> PE pipe must always be cut with a toothed saw or a precision cutting blade, ensuring a clean cut without extra rings. Slanted cuts cause leaks in the socket and reduce service life.</li>\n<li><strong>Lubricating the socket:</strong> Using silicone grease or a special PE grease before tightening the fitting prevents internal surface wear and extends the pipe\'s lifespan.</li>\n<li><strong>Testing:</strong> After installation, the pipe must be held under a pressure 10-15 degrees above the nominal working pressure for at least 2 hours to identify any potential leaks.</li>\n<li><strong>UV protection:</strong> Black pipes are UV-resistant. However, if white or light-colored pipes are used, they must be protected from direct sunlight during the day and coiled on the ground to prevent cracking.</li>\n</ol>\n\n<h2>Matching pipes to agricultural and economic crops</h2>\n<p>The selection of 110 mm pipes should align with your crop plan. For example, in wheat cultivation, where water requirements vary, you can <a href="https://navar-abyari.ir/wheat-irrigation-yield-per-hectare-comprehensive-guide/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">comprehensive guide for increasing irrigated wheat yield</a> to calculate the required flow rate per hectare. Divide this flow rate by the line length to determine the flow rate per meter of pipe. If the flow rate per meter exceeds the optimal range, high pressure drop and a need for a larger pipe size are likely. Conversely, if the flow rate is very low, a 110 mm pipe with a higher SDR (thinner wall) may be more cost-effective.</p>\n\n\n<p>Additionally, when growing various legumes such as barley, attention must be paid to factors affecting seed usage and irrigation levels. Study <a href="https://navar-abyari.ir/barley-seed-quantity-per-hectare-factors/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">factors affecting barley seed rate per hectare</a> It can help in accurately estimating irrigation water requirements and selecting the appropriate size for laterals alongside the 110 mm mainline. This coordination between crop and irrigation increases the overall system efficiency.</p>\n<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="https://navar-abyari.ir/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/navar-article-generated/مشخصات-فنی-لوله-نخدار-110-میلیمتر-راهنمای-انتخاب-کاربرد-عملی.webp" alt="مشخصات فنی لوله نخدار 110 میلیمتر: راهنمای انتخاب - تصویر 2"/><figcaption>product technical specs selection threaded pipe 110 mm</figcaption></figure>\n\n<h2>Frequently Asked Questions (FAQ) about 110 mm pipe</h2>\n<h3>Is 110 mm pipe suitable for lateral lines?</h3>\n<p>Typically, 110 mm pipe is used for mainlines. For laterals, sizes ranging from 50 to 75 mm are more appropriate. Using 110 mm for laterals leads to higher costs and requires more space in the field, making it economically unjustifiable except in cases of very high flow rates.</p>\n\n<h3>What is the service life of PE 110 mm pipe?</h3>\n<p>With good quality and against nominal working pressure, a service life of 50 years or more is specified. However, factors such as UV radiation, soil chemicals, and pressure surges reduce this lifespan. Proper maintenance is the key to preserving this long-term service life.</p>\n\n<h3>What is the difference between 110 mm pipe and 110 SDR pipe?</h3>\n<p>SDR indicates the pipe pressure rating. A 110 mm pipe with SDR 21 withstands higher pressure and has a thicker wall. A 110 mm pipe with SDR 40 has a thinner wall and lower pressure capacity. Selection is based on pump input pressure and farm elevation. On sloped farms, hydrostatic pressures must be included in SDR calculations.</p>\n<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="https://navar-abyari.ir/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/navar-article-generated/مشخصات-فنی-لوله-نخدار-110-میلیمتر-راهنمای-انتخاب-جزئیات-فنی.webp" alt="مشخصات فنی لوله نخدار 110 میلیمتر: راهنمای انتخاب - تصویر 3"/><figcaption>product technical specs selection 110 mm threaded pipe</figcaption></figure>\n\n\n<h2>Summary</h2>\n<p>The 110 mm threaded pipe is the main trunk for many local irrigation systems. Selection based on material, SDR, and connection type directly affects pressure stability, drip emitter performance, and farm economic efficiency. Do not neglect precise pressure drop calculations, and always use standard fittings and PTFE grease. For smaller farms, size 75 may be sufficient, but for larger farms and high flow rates, a 110 mm pipe with appropriate SDR is a smart choice. By adhering to installation and maintenance principles, this investment will serve for decades. Consideration of crop type is also vital in the final selection; to learn about various irrigation line types and per-hectare operations, refer to <a href="https://navar-abyari.ir/%D8%A7%D9%86%D9%88%D8%A7%D8%B9-%D9%86%D9%88%D8%A7%D8%B1-%D8%A2%D8%A8%DB%8C%D8%A7%D8%B1%DB%8C-%D9%88-%D8%B9%D9%85%D9%84%DA%A9%D8%B1%D8%AF-%D9%87%D8%B1%DA%A9%D8%AF%D8%A7%D9%85/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Types of drip lines and per-hectare performance</a> It is recommended.</p>\n<p><strong>Related articles:</strong> D986DAAFD987D8AFD8A7D8B1DB8C D986D988D8A7D8B1 D8AADB8CD9BE D988 D987D8B2DB8CD986D987</p>\n<p><strong>Related articles:</strong> <a href="https://navar-abyari.ir/%D9%86%DA%AF%D9%87%D8%AF%D8%A7%D8%B1%DB%8C-%D9%86%D9%88%D8%A7%D8%B1-%D8%AA%DB%8C%D9%BE-%D9%88-%D9%87%D8%B2%DB%8C%D9%86%D9%87/">D986DAAFD987D8AFD8A7D8B1DB8C D986D988D8A7D8B1 D8AADB8CD9BE D988 D987D8B2DB8CD986D987</a></p>','110 mm HDPE Ribbed Pipe Technical Specifications: A Selection Guide for Irrigation Systems','Selecting the right pipe is the core of your irrigation system. This section provides a technical review of 110 mm threaded pipe, covering its benefits in reducing energy loss and key installation points for extending the system\'s service life.','publish','closed','closed','110mm-hdpe-ribbed-pipe-specs-guide',NOW(),UTC_TIMESTAMP(),0,'',0,'post','',0 WHERE @source_post_id IS NOT NULL AND @translation_id IS NULL AND @slug_conflict IS NULL;
